bcr666 wrote:
> I would like to know people's opinions on searching for traps.  I
> don't usually look for traps, because they are few and far between, so
> I'm not sure if it is worth the time expenditure to search every step
> I take through the dungeon.  On the other hand, I've seen many
> scrolls, cloaks, potions destroyed from towers of flame.

Besides the special case of searching for known traps (in niches, in the
Valley, etc.) there's just one situation where I might search carefully;
if I encounter more than one out-of-depth monster that might got created
by a polymorph trap, in case I don't have MR or polymorph control, then
I will search for the trap to not step into it and ruin my armor.

Otherwise I don't search for traps, because it's time consuming and will
have some dangers, e.g. that you starve more easily.

> How does a ring of searching affect the game?

It will increase the probability that you will find adjacent traps, even
if you don't explicitly search for traps.

If I have a free ring slot available I always wear that ring.

